# Rabbit R1 scroll wheel -> app scroll keys.
#
# The wheel is a Hall-effect encoder reported by the input device "och1970_holl_key"
# (/dev/input/event2) as scancodes 103 (KEY_UP) and 108 (KEY_DOWN). Generic.kl maps
# those to DPAD_UP / DPAD_DOWN, which the framework treats as keyboard navigation:
# after any touch the first press is swallowed just to leave touch mode, and Compose
# then walks focus through every clickable row (with the focus sound) before the key
# reaches the app. Verified on the device 2026-09-14: a direction change cost five or
# six dead ticks, and the first tick after a tap was always lost.
#
# F11 (up) and F10 (down) mean nothing to the framework or to any app here, so every
# detent reaches MainActivity.dispatchKeyEvent, which turns them into wheel ticks.
# The wheel is not a wake source (no WAKE), same as with Generic.kl.
#
# Installed at /data/system/devices/keylayout/och1970_holl_key.kl by install.sh.
# Consequence: outside our app the wheel no longer acts as up/down; the bootloader
# still reads it as volume (that is below Android and unaffected).

key 103   F11
key 108   F10
